THOUGHT: NullAway complains because resolver is @Nullable but is dereferenced without a check. I should either enforce non-null via constructor or handle the null case. Since the constructor already allows @Nullable, the safest fix is to add a null check in resolve and throw a clear exception if resolver is null, avoiding new annotations that might conflict elsewhere. After that, I need to run the compile task to confirm the error count drops by one and no new errors appear.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/libgdx && sed -i '52,54c\  public FileHandle resolve(String fileName) {
    if (resolver == null) {
      throw new IllegalStateException("FileHandleResolver is not set for this AssetLoader");
    }
    return resolver.resolve(fileName);
  }' gdx/src/com/badlogic/gdx/assets/loaders/AssetLoader.java && ./gradlew gdx:compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && grep -n "AssetLoader.java" -n new_build_output.log || tail -n 40 new_build_output.log
```

